{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>They shall not be removed from it.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted in Yoma, chapter בא לו, that the poles never moved from the rings, and whoever removes the poles from the rings transgresses this prohibition. And there further: ״והבאת את הבדים בטבעות״ — teaches that the poles would slide back and forth; one might think they could slip out of the rings — Scripture says, ״לא יסורו ממנו״; one might think they did not move from their place — Scripture says, ״והבאת את הבדים בטבעות״; how so? they slide but do not slip out. And Rashi of blessed memory explained there that the poles were thin in their middle and therefore ״והבאת״ — that is, they would slide back and forth — and thick at their heads, and therefore ״לא יסורו ממנו״ — and this is what is meant by 'they slide but do not slip out.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:04:11.898055509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}